tartAt` assignment AND subsequent click-driven seeks, READ `video.currentTime` first (captures the post-mount value), THEN install the descriptor override (captures subsequent writes). If you override before the initial currentTime read, the underlying setter's effect on the native element is lost.\n  - Asset API extension: adding new media types to `src/app/api/courses/[slug]/assets/[...path]/route.ts` is a one-line change (extend `CONTENT_TYPES`). The same map gates BOTH the GET Content-Type header and the PUT extension allow-list, so adding `.mp4` lets video assets be served with the correct mime type and uploaded via the existing PUT endpoint.\n  - For the YouTube iframe API without loading `youtube/iframe_api`: send raw `{event:'command', func, args}` JSON strings via `iframe.contentWindow.postMessage(..., '*')`. To receive `currentTime`, listen for `message` events from the iframe and parse `{event:'infoDelivery', info:{currentTime}}` payloads. Activate this stream with `addEventListener('onStateChange')` after the iframe fires `onReady`.\n  - `extractYouTubeId` regex `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{11}$` covers all current YouTube IDs but also matches a sample text like `aircAruvnKk` — that's intentional for \"paste either the URL or the ID\" UX. URLs are handled by the `URL()` constructor with explicit host allow-listing (`youtube.com`, `m.youtube.com`, `youtu.be`, `youtube-nocookie.com`).\n---\n\n\n## 2026-05-04 00:30 - US-048\n- Implemented DataTable widget — sortable / filterable / paginated table for inline datasets, results, and comparisons. Click a column header to cycle asc → desc → unsorted (stable, original order preserved). Per-filterable-column filter row: text-contains for `string`, paired min/max number inputs for `number`. Pagination centred below the table (Prev / \"Page X of Y\" / Next) appears only when `rows.length > pageSize`. Numeric cells use `toLocaleString()` for thousand separators; boolean cells render as `✓`/`—`. Sticky `<thead>` inside an `overflow:auto` scroll wrapper (max-height 60vh) so headers stay visible when scrolling many rows.\n- Files added:\n  - `src/widgets/DataTable/{schema.ts, sample.ts, DataTableWidget.tsx, DataTableEditor.tsx}`\n  - `src/widgets/schemas/data-table.json` (regenerated by `npm run build:schemas`)\n  - `courses/datatable-test/{course.json, lessons/scores.json}` — smoke-test course (30 rows × 4 cols, pageSize 10)\n- Files changed:\n  - `src/widgets/registry.ts` — `dataTable` entry (Table icon from lucide-react, `--widget-data-table` accent), `WidgetType` union extended\n  - `src/widgets/schemas/build.ts` — added `data-table` to widgets map\n  - `src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts` — `DataTableSectionSchema` variant added to discriminated union\n  - `src/styles/tokens.css` — `--widget-data-table` CSS var in both light (`#4a6f8a`) + dark (`#94b3d0`) blocks\n  - `src/app/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug]/page.tsx` — wired `DataTableEditor` into `WidgetEditPanel` and added `dataTable` body branch in `SectionRenderer`\n  - `src/lib/schemas/schemas.test.ts` — discriminated-union case for `dataTable` + dedicated `DataTableData` schema tests, `sortRows` tests (asc/desc/unsorted/null-handling/non-mutating), `filterRows` tests (string contains, number range, AND of multiple filters, ignores non-filterable columns, empty filters pass-through)\n  - `src/widgets/schemas/lesson.json` — regenerated\n  - `scripts/ralph/progress.txt` — added 2 codebase patterns (clampedPage instead of setState-in-effect, sticky-thead recipe)\n- Quality checks: `npm run typecheck` clean, `npm test` 7 files / 155 tests pass (added 19 new tests over US-047), `npm run lint` clean in `src/widgets/DataTable/` (only pre-existing errors remain in `claude/design/source/*.jsx` and `scripts/ralph/skills/playwright-skill/*.js`).\n- Browser test (playwright headless on http://localhost:3036/courses/datatable-test/lessons/scores, `/tmp/playwright-test-us-048.js`):\n  - Loaded 30-row × 4-col table, pageSize=10 → \"Page 1 of 3\" indicator visible.\n  - Clicked Score header → ascending sort verified (every cell ≥ previous on page 1: 20,21,23,25,26,28,30,31,33,35).\n  - Clicked again → descending sort verified (69,67,65,64,62,60,59,57,55,54).\n  - Clicked third time → header `data-sort` attribute reverts to `none` (insertion order restored).\n  - Filtered Name column with \"gra\" → summary shows \"Showing 1–1 of 1 (filtered from 30)\", only \"Grace\" visible.\n  - Cleared filter, set Score min=70 → empty state (\"No matching rows\") since sample scores top out at 69, confirming range filter applies.\n  - Clicked Next → \"Page 2 of 3\", row indices start at 10 (verified `[data-testid=\"datatable-cell-10-name\"]` exists), boolean cells render `✓`/`—`. Clicked Prev → returned to Page 1.\n  - Screenshots at `/tmp/us-048-{1-initial,2-sorted-desc,3-filtered,4-numfiltered,5-page2}.png`.\n- **Assumptions made (no human in the loop):**\n  - \"Sort indicator chevron shown next to header label\" — used `ChevronUp`/`ChevronDown` for active asc/desc and a dimmed `ChevronsUpDown` for sortable-but-unsorted columns. Non-sortable columns render as plain `<span>` with no chevron and no button.\n  - \"Numeric columns formatted via `toLocaleString()`\" applied to the user-facing cell rendering only — the underlying row data and sort comparisons use the raw numeric value, so locale-formatted strings like `1,000` don't break `min/max` filter parsing.\n  - Number range filter: blank min OR blank max means \"no bound on that side\"; setting both to blank disables the column filter entirely.\n  - Boolean column filter: AC says \"filter input per filterable column (text contains for string type, range min/max inputs for number type)\" — boolean has no described filter UI, so `filterable: true` on a boolean column degrades gracefully (the column simply renders no filter input). Sample course marks the boolean column `filterable: false` to avoid surprise.\n- **Learnings for future iterations:**","numLines":80,"startLine":1,"totalLines":212}}}
