{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CFwsnRbDLsA78hPkcaFqmE","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Ralph Progress Log\n2\tRotated: Sun May  3 20:56:44 CEST 2026\n3\tPrevious log archived to: archive/progress-2026-05-03-2056.txt\n4\t---\n5\t\n6\t## 2026-05-04 00:50 - US-049\n7\t- Implemented Video widget — embeds YouTube via `<iframe src='youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>?enablejsapi=1&rel=0&modestbranding=1[&start=N][&autoplay=1]'>` (16:9 responsive `aspect-ratio` container) or HTML5 `<video controls>` for MP4. Optional collapsible transcript panel below the player; click a segment to seek the player (postMessage `seekTo` for YouTube, `el.currentTime = N` for MP4). Active segment highlights in `--accent-subtle` driven by `timeupdate` (MP4) or YouTube iframe API `infoDelivery` events polled at 250 ms. Speaker labels rendered as small uppercase prefix per the AC styling. `extractYouTubeId()` accepts: bare 11-char id, `youtu.be/<id>`, `youtube.com/watch?v=<id>` (incl. `m.youtube.com` and `youtube-nocookie.com`), `/embed/<id>`, `/shorts/<id>`.\n8\t- Files added:\n9\t  - `src/widgets/Video/{schema.ts, sample.ts, VideoWidget.tsx, VideoEditor.tsx}`\n10\t  - `src/widgets/schemas/video.json` (regenerated by `npm run build:schemas`)\n11\t  - `courses/video-test/{course.json, lessons/neural-net-intro.json, lessons/mp4-demo.json}` — smoke-test course (YouTube + MP4 lessons)\n12\t- Files changed:\n13\t  - `src/widgets/registry.ts` — `video` entry (Video icon from lucide-react, `--widget-video` accent), `WidgetType` union extended\n14\t  - `src/widgets/schemas/build.ts` — added `video` to widget map\n15\t  - `src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts` — `VideoSectionSchema` variant added to discriminated union\n16\t  - `src/styles/tokens.css` — `--widget-video` CSS var in both light (`#b94a6f`) + dark (`#e08aa8`) blocks\n17\t  - `src/app/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug]/page.tsx` — wired `VideoEditor` into `WidgetEditPanel`, added `video` body branch in `SectionRenderer`\n18\t  - `src/app/api/courses/[slug]/assets/[...path]/route.ts` — extended asset route's `CONTENT_TYPES` map with `.mp4 → video/mp4` and `.webm → video/webm` so course-hosted MP4 files served via the asset API have a correct Content-Type\n19\t  - `src/lib/schemas/schemas.test.ts` — discriminated-union case for `video` + dedicated `VideoData` schema tests + `extractYouTubeId` tests covering id-only, youtu.be, watch?v=, /embed/, /shorts/, mobile/nocookie hosts, and rejection of non-YouTube and bad input\n20\t  - `src/widgets/schemas/lesson.json` — regenerated\n21\t- Quality checks: `npm run typecheck` clean. `npm test` 7 files / 167 tests pass (added 12 new tests: 7 schema + 5 URL parser). `npm run lint` clean in `src/widgets/Video/` (only pre-existing errors remain in `claude/design/source/*.jsx` and `scripts/ralph/skills/playwright-skill/*.js`).\n22\t- Browser test (playwright headless on http://localhost:3049):\n23\t  - **YouTube** (`/tmp/playwright-test-us-049.js` → `/tmp/us-049-1-youtube.png`):\n24\t    - URL `watch?v=aircAruvnKk` rendered as `<iframe src='https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/aircAruvnKk?enablejsapi=1&rel=0&modestbranding=1'>`; `data-yt-id=\"aircAruvnKk\"` confirms parser extracted the id from the URL.\n25\t    - 5 transcript segments rendered; segment 0 shows speaker label `Grant` followed by the text.\n26\t    - Clicked segment index 3 (tStart=32) → `data-active=\"true\"` flipped to that segment within 300 ms (verified via `[data-testid^=\"video-transcript-seg-\"]` query).\n27\t    - Clicked the toggle → `[data-testid=\"video-transcript-list\"]` removed; clicked again → re-rendered.\n28\t    - Note: cross-origin postMessage on `iframe.contentWindow` cannot be intercepted from the parent, so seek verification on YouTube is via observable side-effects (active flip, no JS error). The seek mechanism itself is exercised end-to-end on the MP4 path where currentTime IS observable.\n29\t  - **MP4** (`/tmp/playwright-test-us-049-mp4.js` → `/tmp/us-049-2-mp4.png`):\n30\t    - `/api/courses/video-test/assets/sample.mp4` 404s (no real asset committed) but the `<video>` element is still rendered with `controls`, `src`, `autoplay=false`. The 404 is expected and documented in the test.\n31\t    - `startAt: 5` → on mount `video.currentTime` reads `5` (verified BEFORE installing the descriptor override).\n32\t    - Installed a `currentTime` setter spy → clicked segment 1 (tStart=10) → spy captured `[10]`.\n33\t    - Speaker label `Narrator` appears on segment 1.\n34\t- **Assumptions made (no human in the loop):**\n35\t  - \"Embed via youtube-nocookie.com\" interpreted as the privacy-enhanced domain regardless of input host. Both `youtube.com/watch?v=...` and `youtu.be/...` URLs map to `youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>` for embedding.\n36\t  - YouTube iframe `enablejsapi=1` is set by default so postMessage seek works without authoring intervention. `rel=0&modestbranding=1` reduce branding/related-video chrome — these aren't in the AC but are standard housekeeping for educational embeds.\n37\t  - Active segment detection: a segment is active when `tStart ≤ currentTime` AND (`tEnd` is undefined OR `currentTime < tEnd`). When a segment has no `tEnd`, the active range extends to the next segment's `tStart`, so the final segment stays active to the end of the video.\n38\t  - Transcript expanded by default. Hidden transcript with a toggle-to-show button is more discoverable than open-by-default-but-collapsible, but the AC says \"collapsible\" not \"collapsed\", and a 3-row transcript looks weird collapsed. Kept it open by default; toggle works both directions.\n39\t  - MP4 path: `<video controls>` rather than a custom player. AC says \"HTML5 `<video controls>` tag\" — taken literally.\n40\t  - YouTube currentTime tracking: poll the iframe at 250 ms via `getCurrentTime` postMessage; the response arrives via `infoDelivery` event listener. This is the documented YouTube IFrame API contract; alternative would be loading the official `iframe_api.js` script, but the `enablejsapi=1` URL param + raw postMessage is sufficient for the seek+highlight use case the AC describes.\n41\t- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n42\t  - Cross-origin iframes (YouTube, Vimeo, etc.) prevent the parent from spying on or replacing methods on `iframe.contentWindow` — Chromium throws `SecurityError: Failed to set a named property 'postMessage' on 'Window': Blocked a frame with origin \"...\" from accessing a cross-origin frame`. For seek/play tests on third-party embeds, prefer observable side-effects (DOM state, our own component state) or test the seek path through MP4/HTML5 video where `currentTime` is observable from the parent.\n43\t  - Stubbing `<video>.currentTime` in playwright: `Object.defineProperty(v, 'currentTime', { get, set, configurable: true })` works AFTER the React component has done its initial assignment. To verify both an initial `startAt` assignment AND subsequent click-driven seeks, READ `video.currentTime` first (captures the post-mount value), THEN install the descriptor override (captures subsequent writes). If you override before the initial currentTime read, the underlying setter's effect on the native element is lost.\n44\t  - Asset API extension: adding new media types to `src/app/api/courses/[slug]/assets/[...path]/route.ts` is a one-line change (extend `CONTENT_TYPES`). The same map gates BOTH the GET Content-Type header and the PUT extension allow-list, so adding `.mp4` lets video assets be served with the correct mime type and uploaded via the existing PUT endpoint.\n45\t  - For the YouTube iframe API without loading `youtube/iframe_api`: send raw `{event:'command', func, args}` JSON strings via `iframe.contentWindow.postMessage(..., '*')`. To receive `currentTime`, listen for `message` events from the iframe and parse `{event:'infoDelivery', info:{currentTime}}` payloads. Activate this stream with `addEventListener('onStateChange')` after the iframe fires `onReady`.