{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U4FxJkTTCGws5PALbzh7mT","type":"tool_result","content":"200\t  - `src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts` — added `ParametricExplorerSectionSchema` variant to discriminated union\n201\t  - `src/styles/tokens.css` — new `--widget-parametric-explorer` CSS var in light + dark blocks\n202\t  - `src/app/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug]/page.tsx` — wired `ParametricExplorerEditor` into `WidgetEditPanel` and the `parametricExplorer` body branch in `SectionRenderer`\n203\t  - `src/lib/schemas/schemas.test.ts` — added schema tests (minimal-valid, select+toggle, debounceMs, unknown-outputType reject) and param-injection serialization tests (slider→number, toggle→bool, select→string, mixed)\n204\t  - `src/widgets/schemas/lesson.json` — regenerated\n205\t- Quality checks: `npm run typecheck` clean, `npm test` 7 files / 116 tests pass, `npm run lint` only pre-existing errors in `claude/design/source/*.jsx` and `scripts/ralph/skills/playwright-skill/*.js` (no new errors in `src/`).\n206\t- Browser test (playwright headless on http://localhost:3008): plot-mode lesson dragged slider 1 → 4.5, plot redrew within debounce (verified by `<img>` src change); value-mode dragged 3 → 5, value text updated 9 → 25. Screenshots at `/tmp/us-045-{plot-initial,plot-after-drag,value-after-drag}.png`.\n207\t- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n208\t  - Pyodide takes a noticeable second (~2-5s) to lazy-install matplotlib on first `runWithPlotParam` — first plot blocks until install + setupCode + renderCode + figure savefig finish. Allow generous timeout in playwright (`waitForSelector('[data-testid=\"pexp-plot\"]', { timeout: 120_000 })`).\n209\t  - The `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect` rule catches `void asyncFn()` even when setState is post-await. Gate with a one-shot `useRef(false)` flag, which the rule treats as a one-time subscription pattern (mirrors GaussDemo's `pendingSigmaRef` gate).\n210\t  - When testing back-to-back lesson pages with Turbopack, the dev server can hang after one playwright run completes — `curl` to any route will then time out. Fix: kill the dev server and restart it on a different port between attempts.\n211\t---"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"951b4940-59c9-45a3-ba97-d8bc93a78325","uuid":"a5876265-662e-4479-a464-323ba9825c0e","timestamp":"2026-05-04T00:48:50.198Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/nukeemann/projects/ai_lecturer/.worktrees/US-050/scripts/ralph/progress.txt","content":"  - `src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts` — added `ParametricExplorerSectionSchema` variant to discriminated union\n  - `src/styles/tokens.css` — new `--widget-parametric-explorer` CSS var in light + dark blocks\n  - `src/app/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug]/page.tsx` — wired `ParametricExplorerEditor` into `WidgetEditPanel` and the `parametricExplorer` body branch in `SectionRenderer`\n  - `src/lib/schemas/schemas.test.ts` — added schema tests (minimal-valid, select+toggle, debounceMs, unknown-outputType reject) and param-injection serialization tests (slider→number, toggle→bool, select→string, mixed)\n  - `src/widgets/schemas/lesson.json` — regenerated\n- Quality checks: `npm run typecheck` clean, `npm test` 7 files / 116 tests pass, `npm run lint` only pre-existing errors in `claude/design/source/*.jsx` and `scripts/ralph/skills/playwright-skill/*.js` (no new errors in `src/`).\n- Browser test (playwright headless on http://localhost:3008): plot-mode lesson dragged slider 1 → 4.5, plot redrew within debounce (verified by `<img>` src change); value-mode dragged 3 → 5, value text updated 9 → 25. Screenshots at `/tmp/us-045-{plot-initial,plot-after-drag,value-after-drag}.png`.\n- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n  - Pyodide takes a noticeable second (~2-5s) to lazy-install matplotlib on first `runWithPlotParam` — first plot blocks until install + setupCode + renderCode + figure savefig finish. Allow generous timeout in playwright (`waitForSelector('[data-testid=\"pexp-plot\"]', { timeout: 120_000 })`).\n  - The `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect` rule catches `void asyncFn()` even when setState is post-await. Gate with a one-shot `useRef(false)` flag, which the rule treats as a one-time subscription pattern (mirrors GaussDemo's `pendingSigmaRef` gate).\n  - When testing back-to-back lesson pages with Turbopack, the dev server can hang after one playwright run completes — `curl` to any route will then time out. Fix: kill the dev server and restart it on a different port between attempts.\n---","numLines":12,"startLine":200,"totalLines":212}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_017oDhMgyyLujxmiTNv6upSk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HeXCM22nxc81ktbR8P5VgV","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> /home/nukeemann/projects/ai_lecturer/.worktrees/US-050/scripts/ralph/progress.txt <<'EOF'\n\n\n## 2026-05-04 02:48 - US-050\n- Implemented Image widget — `<figure>` containing an `<img>` plus optional `<figcaption>` with caption text + attribution (linked when `attribution.url` is present, else plain text). `maxWidth` is applied via a wrapper `<div>` inside the figure (not on the `<img>`) so the img stays `width:100%` of the wrapper, preserving the existing `objectFit:contain` rendering. ImageEditor follows US-023 pattern (URL text input + alt + caption + attribution.text + attribution.url + maxWidth) with no upload button — the prefetch flow on save is server-side and transparent to the author.\n- Server-side prefetch helper (`src/lib/server/imagePrefetch.ts`):\n  - `prefetchImageToCourse(slug, url)` downloads an external (`http`/`https`) image into `courses/<slug>/assets/images/<sha256(url).slice(0,16)>.<ext>`, returning `{ localSrc, filePath, fetched }` or `null` on failure. Idempotent — short-circuits when the URL extension is recognised AND the candidate file already exists; otherwise falls back to the response `Content-Type` header to determine the extension. Bounded by a 15s `AbortController` timeout and a 25 MB cap.\n  - `prefetchLessonImages(slug, lesson)` walks `lesson.sections`, prefetches every Image section whose `data.src` `isExternalImageUrl(...)`, rewrites `data.src` to the local API path, and returns `{ lesson, failures: ImagePrefetchFailure[] }`. Local paths and non-image sections are untouched.\n  - The lesson PUT route (`src/app/api/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug]/route.ts`) now calls `prefetchLessonImages` after Zod validation, atomic-writes the rewritten lesson, and returns `{ ...lesson, warning: { imagePrefetchFailures } }` when fetches fail (200 still — graceful degradation per AC).\n- Files added:\n  - `src/widgets/Image/{schema.ts, sample.ts, ImageWidget.tsx, ImageEditor.tsx}`\n  - `src/widgets/schemas/image.json` (regenerated by `npm run build:schemas`)\n  - `src/lib/server/imagePrefetch.ts` (helpers) + `src/lib/server/imagePrefetch.test.ts` (20 tests)\n  - `courses/image-test/{course.json, lessons/local-image.json, assets/images/sample.png}` — smoke-test course with a 16x16 PNG referenced via the local API path\n- Files changed:\n  - `src/widgets/registry.ts` — `image` entry (lucide-react `Image` icon, `--widget-image` accent), `WidgetType` union extended with `'image'`\n  - `src/widgets/schemas/build.ts` — added `image: ImageDataSchema` to widgets map\n  - `src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts` — `ImageSectionSchema` variant added to the discriminated union\n  - `src/styles/tokens.css` — `--widget-image: #6f8a4a` (light) / `#b3d094` (dark) — sage-leaning accent so it doesn't collide with existing rails\n  - `src/app/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug]/route.ts` — PUT integrates `prefetchLessonImages`, surfaces `warning.imagePrefetchFailures` on partial failure\n  - `src/app/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug]/page.tsx` — `ImageEditor` wired into `WidgetEditPanel` and `SectionRenderer` with an `image-edit-btn` pencil\n  - `src/lib/schemas/schemas.test.ts` — discriminated-union case for `image` + dedicated ImageData tests (minimal, full, attribution-text-only, empty-alt, missing-alt, empty-src, bad attribution.url, empty attribution.text, isExternalImageUrl http/https vs relative/data/file)\n  - `src/widgets/schemas/lesson.json` — regenerated to include the new `image` variant\n- Quality checks: `npm run build:schemas` clean. `npm run typecheck` clean. `npm test` 8 files / 196 tests pass (added 30 new tests: 9 ImageData schema + 1 union + 4 hashUrlToFilename + 5 inferExt + 7 prefetchImageToCourse + 4 prefetchLessonImages). `npm run lint` clean in all new files (185 pre-existing problems remain in `claude/design/source/*.jsx` and `scripts/ralph/skills/playwright-skill/*.js`).\n- Browser test (playwright headless on http://localhost:3050, `/tmp/playwright-test-us-050.js`):\n  - Light + dark themes both render `<figure>` → `<img src=/api/courses/image-test/assets/images/sample.png alt=\"...\">` with `naturalWidth=16, naturalHeight=16, complete=true`.\n  - Caption renders with the expected text. Attribution link renders with `href=https://example.com/us-050`, `target=_blank`, `rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`.\n  - Wrapper div applies `max-width: 320px` from the lesson JSON (verified via `[data-image-figure] div[style*=\"max-width\"]`).\n  - End-to-end prefetch via PUT: added a section with `src=https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/47/PNG_transparency_demonstration_1.png`, sent PUT, response body's new section src came back as `/api/courses/image-test/assets/images/d2a66aba23504841.png` — happy path verified live. Test reverts the lesson + the leftover prefetched cache file is removed before commit so the committed course only contains the deliberate 95-byte sample.png.\n  - Screenshots: `/tmp/us-050-{light,dark}.png`.\n- **Assumptions made (no human in the loop):**\n  - Filename = `sha256(url).slice(0,16)` — the AC is explicit. The same hash + extension means re-saving the same external URL is idempotent. If two URLs collide on the 16-hex prefix (cosmically unlikely), the second one will overwrite the first; not a real-world concern at this prefix length but flagging.\n  - Extension resolution priority: URL pathname extension first (lets us short-circuit cache hits without a network call), then `Content-Type` header on the response. If neither yields a supported extension, the prefetch fails and the original URL is preserved.\n  - Supported extensions: `.png .jpg .jpeg .svg .webp .gif` — matches the existing asset route's `CONTENT_TYPES` map (which handles GET serving + PUT upload allow-list). `.gif` is included even though the AC doesn't mention animated content because the asset route already serves it.\n  - Asset API \"extension\" requirement (AC item 8): the existing `[...path]` catch-all route already serves `assets/images/<file>` — the catch-all and its `assertSafeAssetPath` accept multi-part paths with no changes needed. The `image/png|jpeg|svg+xml|webp|gif` content types are already in the route's map (added pre-MVP). Documented as a no-op but verified end-to-end (sample.png served with `Content-Type: image/png`, browser loaded it with `naturalWidth=16`).\n  - Failed fetch returns 200 with `warning.imagePrefetchFailures: [{url, reason}]`. The AC says \"log warning, keep original URL, return 200 with a warning field\" — interpreted as \"warning sits under a `warning` key in the response body, alongside the usual lesson fields\". Server-side `console.warn` is also emitted per failure.\n  - `maxWidth` is applied to a wrapper `<div>` inside `<figure>` rather than directly on the `<img>` because the styled `<img>` uses `width: 100%` for proper centering; if maxWidth went on the img, the figure wrapper would need different styling for caption alignment. The wrapper-div approach matches PlotImage's styling spirit (figure → img → optional caption) and tested correctly in both themes.\n- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n  - Adding a server-side post-validation hook into the lesson PUT route is straightforward — call your transform after `LessonSchema.safeParse(body)` succeeds, then `atomicWriteJson(file, transformed)`. If the response shape needs extra info (like prefetch warnings), spread the lesson and add a `warning` key — `LessonSchema` (z.object) silently strips unknown keys on next read so it doesn't leak into persistence.\n  - `Object.assign(fn, { get calls() { return calls; } })` does NOT preserve a getter on the destination — Object.assign reads source values and writes them as data properties, so the getter fires once at assign time and the destination has a frozen 0. Use `type FakeFetch = typeof fetch & { calls: number }` and `fn.calls = 0` after defining the function, then mutate via `fn.calls += 1`. (Hit this exact bug while writing the prefetch idempotency test.)\n  - Image asset GETs go through `/api/courses/<slug>/assets/<...path>` — the `[...path]` catch-all already serves arbitrary subdirectories like `assets/images/<file>`, no route changes are needed when introducing a new asset subdirectory. New media types still need a one-line addition to `CONTENT_TYPES` though.\n  - Schema-driven discriminated unions: when adding a new variant, the change list is always: (1) new schema in `widgets/<Name>/schema.ts`, (2) build.ts widget map entry, (3) NameSectionSchema in `lib/schemas/lesson.ts` AND added to the `discriminatedUnion` array, (4) `WidgetType` union + `widgetRegistry` entry, (5) tokens.css var in both themes, (6) page.tsx `WidgetEditPanel` branch + `SectionRenderer` branch + Editor import. Skipping any one of (1)-(3) makes the lesson save fail Zod; skipping (4)-(6) makes the widget unrenderable. (Same checklist as DataTable/Video before.)\n  - For idempotency-style integration tests against real filesystem behaviour: use `fs.mkdtemp(os.tmpdir() + ...)` plus `process.env.COURSES_ROOT_OVERRIDE` (already supported by `coursesRoot()`). `beforeEach` creates a fresh temp root, `afterEach` `fs.rm({recursive:true, force:true})` it. No need to mock fs.\n---\nEOF\necho \"appended\"","description":"Append progress entry"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1027,"cache_read_input_tokens":169737,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1027},"output_tokens":68,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"951b4940-59c9-45a3-ba97-d8bc93a78325","uuid":"03de0fa3-d535-4d12-8e38-a7ec3ea2cd4f"}
